    "gemini_btc5m_15m": {
      "spread_med": 0.28,
      "touch_depth": 217,
      "touch_move_per_min": 5.18,
      "reach120": 24.4,
      "median_reach_s": 72
    },
    "reading": "Three distinct failures, and spread does not separate them. Gemini is WIDE: the complement sits 28c from the trading. PMUS sports are TIGHT BUT FROZEN: the spread is half a cent -- BETTER than L5's source -- but the touch holds ~3,951 contracts and is replaced only 0.6 times a minute, so a 0.01 quote is behind a wall that does not move. Polymarket International is tight AND churning: only ~65 contracts at the touch, replaced ~4.9 times a minute, so the queue drains and the book comes back. QUEUE TURNOVER -- depth divided by touch replacement -- separates all three where spread does not."
  },
